      </h2>

      <div class="divide-y divide-[#e2e4e8] dark:divide-[#23252a] border border-[#e2e4e8] dark:border-[#23252a] bg-white dark:bg-[#0f1011] rounded-[12px] px-5 sm:px-6 shadow-sm">
        <details class="group py-4" open>
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>What is a font finder?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            A font finder is an optical typography tool that analyzes text inside an image, screenshot, or graphic to determine the typeface name, typographic style, and font family. FreeFontFinderAI identifies fonts locally and matches them with verified open-source Google Fonts alternatives.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>How can I find a font from an image?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            Simply drag and drop or upload your image file (PNG, JPG, or WebP) into the Font Finder upload dropzone above. The tool isolates the text, extracts letterform contours, and instantly displays the highest-confidence matching font families along with direct Google Fonts links and copy-ready CSS embed snippets.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>Can I identify a font from a screenshot?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            Yes. You can paste a screenshot directly into the tool using <code class="text-[#ff4d00] dark:text-[#e4f222] font-mono bg-[#f1f3f6] dark:bg-[#161718] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-[#e2e4e8] dark:border-[#23252a]">Ctrl+V</code> (or <code class="text-[#ff4d00] dark:text-[#e4f222] font-mono bg-[#f1f3f6] dark:bg-[#161718] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-[#e2e4e8] dark:border-[#23252a]">Cmd+V</code> on Mac) or upload a clipped screenshot file. For the most accurate identification, ensure the text in the screenshot is sharp, clear, and horizontally aligned. You can also use our dedicated <a href="/tools/screenshot-font-finder" class="text-[#ff4d00] dark:text-[#e4f222] hover:underline font-medium">Screenshot Font Finder</a>.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>Is the font finder free?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            Yes, FreeFontFinderAI is 100% free with unlimited scans. There are no credit cards, subscriptions, paywalls, or account registrations required. All matched Google Fonts are open-source and free for both personal and commercial use under the SIL Open Font License.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>How does image-based font identification work?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            The tool uses in-browser optical analysis running on HTML5 Canvas and WebGL. It detects text lines, binarizes the raster pixels, traces glyph contours, measures typographic ratios (x-height, stroke weight, aperture, serifs), and computes Euclidean geometric distance against thousands of pre-calculated font vector models in under 150 milliseconds.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>Can I find free alternatives to a font?</span>
            <span class="text-[12px] font-mono text-[#64748b] dark:text-[#8a8f98] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&darr;</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-[#475569] dark:text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed">
            Yes. When an image contains a paid commercial typeface (such as Helvetica, Futura, Gotham, or Didot), Font Finder detects its visual letterform traits and automatically suggests the closest 100% free, open-source Google Fonts alternatives. You can also explore our <a href="/tools/commercial-alternative" class="text-[#ff4d00] dark:text-[#e4f222] hover:underline font-medium">Commercial Font Alternatives Tool</a>.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-[510] text-[#08090a] dark:text-[#ffffff] hover:text-[#ff4d00] dark:hover:text-[#e4f222] list-none transition-colors">
            <span>Can I identify cursive or handwritten fonts?</span>
